WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.990
<v Maya>Welcome to part six, the final part.

2
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.910
<v Maya>We have two factors so far.

3
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.580
<v Maya>Stimulus per set, and stimulus retention.

4
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:16.160
<v Maya>Today, factor three, the determinants of frequency, then the ideal set ranges, the studies, the sample programmes, and a rapid fire quiz.

5
00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:17.520
<v Dev>Let's go.

6
00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.230
<v Maya>There are two determinants.

7
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.680
<v Maya>Hypertrophy is growth in the cell size of the muscle.

8
00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:25.340
<v Maya>Atrophy is reduction in the cell size.

9
00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:26.830
<v Maya>Two abbreviations.

10
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.560
<v Maya>GAS is general adaptation syndrome, how the body adapts in general.

11
00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:35.240
<v Maya>And MyoPS is myofibrillar protein synthesis.

12
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:40.020
<v Maya>Myo means muscle, specifically the myofibril, an element inside the muscle.

13
00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:44.280
<v Maya>Inside it are sarcomeres with the proteins myosin and actin.

14
00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:48.460
<v Maya>Hypertrophy here is the building of these contractile proteins.

15
00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.280
<v Dev>So when does it build?

16
00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:58.620
<v Maya>After you train a muscle, whether with one set or six, hypertrophy, the MyoPS elevation, continues for the first forty eight hours.

17
00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:01.370
<v Maya>After forty eight hours, atrophy begins.

18
00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.280
<v Dev>Is there a picture for that?

19
00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:04.730
<v Maya>The ball analogy.

20
00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.940
<v Maya>Imagine a big rubber ball shot upward by a gun.

21
00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:10.480
<v Maya>It rises, curves and starts to fall.

22
00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:14.610
<v Maya>The goal is to never let the ball, the hypertrophy curve, touch the ground.

23
00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.720
<v Maya>Before it falls, shoot it up again.

24
00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:19.690
<v Maya>The ball rises for forty eight hours, then falls.

25
00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:25.500
<v Maya>For any programme, do you shoot again at the last minute, a little earlier, or at the exact moment the fall starts?

26
00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:29.050
<v Maya>Compare three people, each doing six sets a week for the muscle.

27
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.690
<v Maya>Six sets once a week, push pull legs type.

28
00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.750
<v Maya>Three plus three sets twice a week, upper lower type.

29
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.910
<v Maya>And two sets three times a week, full body type.

30
00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:39.620
<v Maya>Day one is a Monday.

31
00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:41.620
<v Dev>Start with once a week.

32
00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.960
<v Maya>Six sets, two point zero zero.

33
00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.670
<v Maya>It is not in the pocket straight after the gym.

34
00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.570
<v Maya>It builds over forty eight hours, then the ball falls.

35
00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:53.480
<v Maya>With no more training it reaches zero on day ten, six plus four.

36
00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:56.140
<v Maya>He trains again on day eight, next Monday.

37
00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:59.280
<v Maya>So he avoided some atrophy but still faced a lot.

38
00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:04.280
<v Maya>The curve then goes higher than two, because he carries a bank balance from the previous week.

39
00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:06.320
<v Maya>That is how muscle is built.

40
00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:07.830
<v Dev>Twice a week?

41
00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.290
<v Maya>Three sets, one point six one each.

42
00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:12.460
<v Maya>Peak at forty eight hours, Wednesday.

43
00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:15.180
<v Maya>Zero would be on day seven, three plus four.

44
00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:19.420
<v Maya>But he trains again on Thursday, day four, so he faces less atrophy.

45
00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:26.310
<v Maya>The new session starts from the carried balance and rises again for forty eight hours, to Saturday, then drops over the weekend.

46
00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:29.860
<v Maya>Overall his curve stays higher than the once a week curve.

47
00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.870
<v Dev>And three times a week?

48
00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.330
<v Maya>Two sets, one point three nine each.

49
00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.040
<v Maya>Forty eight hours after Monday is Wednesday, the next training day.

50
00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:42.870
<v Maya>Atrophy was supposed to start, but he shoots the ball up again at that exact moment.

51
00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:47.920
<v Maya>After Wednesday the window ends Friday, a training day, and after Friday it ends Sunday.

52
00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:53.930
<v Maya>So the blessing in disguise of full body is that the day atrophy would begin is the day of the next session.

53
00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.700
<v Maya>Only the weekend rest day brings some drop.

54
00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:59.160
<v Dev>How would I compare them at a glance?

55
00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:01.300
<v Maya>Count atrophy days in the figure.

56
00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:07.210
<v Maya>Five days a week for once a week, three days for twice, and just one day, the weekend, for three times.

57
00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:10.230
<v Maya>Each panel has its own scale, so compare the shapes.

58
00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:15.040
<v Maya>That is why the full body lifter, even with two sets, always stays near the top.

59
00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.250
<v Maya>Pause and think.

60
00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:21.840
<v Maya>On which day does the once a week lifter with six sets hit zero, and what day does he train again?

61
00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:23.940
<v Dev>Day ten, sets plus four.

62
00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:26.360
<v Dev>And day eight, so before zero.

63
00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:27.350
<v Maya>Correct.

64
00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.310
<v Maya>Recap.

65
00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:31.950
<v Maya>Hypertrophy lasts forty eight hours, then atrophy starts.

66
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.750
<v Maya>Full body retrains exactly when atrophy would begin.

67
00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.720
<v Dev>Now the final column?

68
00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:38.610
<v Maya>Yes.

69
00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:44.080
<v Maya>The ideal main sets per muscle per session, with an upper limit to avoid damage and fatigue.

70
00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:47.940
<v Maya>Three times a week, full body, one to two sets, maximum three.

71
00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:51.770
<v Maya>Twice a week, upper lower, two to three sets, maximum five.

72
00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:56.320
<v Maya>Once a week, push pull legs or bro, six to eight sets, do not cross ten.

73
00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:57.340
<v Dev>Hook?

74
00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:58.690
<v Maya>One, two, three.

75
00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:01.060
<v Maya>Frequency three, sets one to two.

76
00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:03.480
<v Maya>Frequency two, sets two to three.

77
00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:05.800
<v Maya>Frequency one, sets six to eight.

78
00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:08.190
<v Maya>And if frequency is high, stay at the low end.

79
00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:14.170
<v Maya>A quick tour of the published studies, redrawn in your notes from the charts, so treat values as approximate.

80
00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.620
<v Maya>First, recovery against number of sets.

81
00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:24.330
<v Maya>For several studies, the day strength returned to baseline after a workout of six to fifteen RM, taken to failure at least once.

82
00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:27.680
<v Maya>The relationship is roughly linear, more sets, more time.

83
00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:31.220
<v Maya>The chart's conclusions are the three rows of the master table.

84
00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:39.230
<v Maya>Probably recover from three sets within forty eight hours, four to five sets within seventy two hours, and ten to twelve sets within a week.

85
00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.820
<v Dev>Where does the stimulus table come from?

86
00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:45.700
<v Maya>A meta-analysis of resistance training volume and muscle growth.

87
00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:50.870
<v Maya>It found that to double the hypertrophy of one set per workout you need about six sets.

88
00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:58.690
<v Maya>The inverted U shapes may be caused by muscle damage, which is deducted differently for easily and less easily damaged muscles.

89
00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:01.330
<v Dev>Which muscles are easily damaged?

90
00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:05.800
<v Maya>A study with young untrained males did nine eccentric exercises.

91
00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:11.750
<v Maya>Strength dropped most for the pectoralis major, biceps and triceps, and those recovered slowest.

92
00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.860
<v Maya>The drop was smallest for the quadriceps and calves.

93
00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:18.190
<v Maya>So the best frequency may differ between muscle groups.

94
00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:19.640
<v Dev>And retention?

95
00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:24.670
<v Maya>Maintenance research shows three sets once a week gives no gains and no losses.

96
00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:36.550
<v Maya>The stimulus of one point six one disappears over the five days after the forty eight hour period, so about zero point three two is lost per day, one point six one divided by five.

97
00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.870
<v Maya>One set once a week is expected to be insufficient.

98
00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.000
<v Maya>The conclusion, frequency matters.

99
00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:43.990
<v Maya>The samples are only samples.

100
00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:45.430
<v Maya>Do not copy them.

101
00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:53.540
<v Maya>Real programmes come from knowing the client, their goals, strengths, weaknesses, likes, time, preferred frequency and medical concerns.

102
00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:56.700
<v Maya>No programme is best unless built for that client.

103
00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:01.150
<v Maya>The samples show main sets only, with one or two warm-up sets before.

104
00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.560
<v Dev>Sample one?

105
00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:08.050
<v Maya>Full body, Monday, Wednesday, Friday, with Monday and Wednesday exercises alternating.

106
00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:15.800
<v Maya>Monday has squats two, leg curl two, calf one, supported row three, flat chest press three, lateral raise two, biceps curl two.

107
00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:25.280
<v Maya>Wednesday has leg extension two, stiff leg deadlift two, calf one, lat pulldown three, incline press three, shoulder press two, triceps extension two.

108
00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:28.870
<v Maya>Friday repeats Monday, and the next Monday repeats Wednesday.

109
00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:32.470
<v Maya>That is an assumption, since the notes show only two columns.

110
00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:34.190
<v Dev>What do I learn from it?

111
00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:35.810
<v Maya>Count synergists.

112
00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:40.050
<v Maya>Triceps have no direct exercise on Monday, but work in the presses.

113
00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:42.960
<v Maya>The biceps work as synergists in the pulldown.

114
00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:46.610
<v Maya>Frequency counts every exercise where the muscle works.

115
00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:48.090
<v Dev>Sample two?

116
00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:49.160
<v Maya>Upper lower.

117
00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:56.490
<v Maya>Monday upper, Tuesday lower, Wednesday off or cardio, Thursday upper, Friday lower, Saturday off or cardio, Sunday off.

118
00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:58.660
<v Maya>Upper has eleven exercises.

119
00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:11.380
<v Maya>Flat press one, incline press one, pec deck one, shoulder press one, supported row two, wide grip pulldown two, high row one, shrugs one, lateral raise two, preacher curl two, triceps extension two.

120
00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:12.690
<v Maya>Lower has eight.

121
00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:20.870
<v Maya>Squats one, deadlifts one, lunges one, leg extension two, hip thrusts two, calf raises three, leg curl three, toe raises two.

122
00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:23.580
<v Dev>What does a dedicated upper day give?

123
00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:24.430
<v Maya>Room.

124
00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:34.190
<v Maya>You can train all heads of the pectoralis major on one day, flat for the sternocostal and abdominal heads, incline for the clavicular, and add isolation.

125
00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:40.220
<v Maya>The deltoid gets shoulder press, high row and lateral raise, one plus one plus two, so four sets.

126
00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:44.500
<v Maya>Biceps and triceps also work in rows, presses and pulldowns.

127
00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:48.670
<v Maya>The lower day has room for the tibialis anterior with toe raises.

128
00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:50.340
<v Maya>Five things to remember.

129
00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:57.770
<v Maya>One, hypertrophy lasts forty eight hours after training, then atrophy starts, so retrain before the ball hits the ground.

130
00:07:57.820 --> 00:08:04.560
<v Dev>Two, full body retrains exactly when atrophy would begin, so even two sets keep you near the top.

131
00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:10.760
<v Maya>Three, ideal sets: one to two at three times a week, two to three at twice, six to eight at once a week.

132
00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:14.880
<v Dev>Four, upper limits come from muscle damage, and muscles differ.

133
00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:19.370
<v Maya>Five, frequency is per muscle, and real programmes depend on the client.

134
00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:22.100
<v Maya>Time for a rapid fire quiz of twelve.

135
00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:23.030
<v Dev>Ready.

136
00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:25.900
<v Dev>Question one, what does number of sets mean?

137
00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:29.250
<v Maya>Main sets per muscle per session, not warm-up sets.

138
00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:32.430
<v Dev>Two, what do three, two and once a week match?

139
00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:34.910
<v Maya>Thrice a week, twice a week and once a week.

140
00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:41.960
<v Maya>With forty eight hours, seventy two hours and one week of recovery, for one to three, four to five and more than five sets.

141
00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:43.270
<v Maya>Question three.

142
00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:46.080
<v Maya>Which four are the objectives of scheduling?

143
00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:50.910
<v Dev>Linear progression, comprehensive, minimum overlap, avoid overtraining.

144
00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.180
<v Maya>Question four.

145
00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:54.840
<v Maya>What do the three rest day recoveries cover?

146
00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:58.940
<v Dev>Musculoskeletal, nervous system, immune system.

147
00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:00.300
<v Maya>Question five.

148
00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.530
<v Maya>Name the weight training day steps.

149
00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:09.560
<v Dev>General warm-up, mobility drill, specific warm-up set, prep sets, main sets, static passive stretching.

150
00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:10.860
<v Maya>Question six.

151
00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:13.210
<v Maya>On a combined day, which goes first?

152
00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:17.350
<v Dev>Weights, then cardio, with one static stretch at the very end.

153
00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:18.680
<v Maya>Question seven.

154
00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:22.390
<v Maya>What is the relationship between frequency and intensity?

155
00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:25.870
<v Dev>Frequency is proportional to one over intensity.

156
00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:28.550
<v Dev>High intensity, low frequency.

157
00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:29.790
<v Maya>Question eight.

158
00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:33.340
<v Maya>The net stimulus after two sets, and the set three addition?

159
00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:36.570
<v Dev>One point three nine, and zero point two two.

160
00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:37.840
<v Maya>Question nine.

161
00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:40.370
<v Maya>How many sets double the stimulus of one?

162
00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:43.480
<v Dev>Six sets, giving two point zero zero.

163
00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:44.740
<v Maya>Question ten.

164
00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:46.840
<v Maya>When does stimulus reach zero?

165
00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:50.960
<v Dev>Day equals sets plus four, with the training day as day one.

166
00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:52.330
<v Maya>Question eleven.

167
00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.960
<v Maya>Net weekly stimulus for the three splits?

168
00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:59.890
<v Dev>Four point one seven, three point two two, and two point zero zero.

169
00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:01.260
<v Maya>Question twelve.

170
00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:04.670
<v Maya>How long does MyoPS stay raised, and what follows?

171
00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:08.000
<v Dev>About forty eight hours, then atrophy begins.

172
00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:09.210
<v Maya>That is a wrap.

173
00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:11.680
<v Maya>Well done for listening all the way through.

174
00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:15.560
<v Maya>Review your notes, check the differences with your course material, and good luck.

